   "title": "Apple Picking",
   "level": 1,
   "statement": "<p>Ten apples hang on a tree, each at some height. A girl can reach up to a certain height with her hand, and she also has a stool 30 cm tall to stand on. She can pick an apple if its height is at most her reach plus 30. How many of the ten apples can she pick?</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds 10 integers: the heights of the apples in centimetres. The second line holds one integer: the highest point she can touch without the stool.</p>",
   "output": "<p>One integer: the number of apples she can pick.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>Apple heights are between 100 and 200; her reach is between 100 and 120.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "100 200 150 140 129 134 167 198 200 111\n110\n",
     "out": "5\n",
     "why": "<p>With the stool she reaches 140, and five apples hang at 140 or lower.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Work out the highest point she can reach with the stool once, then count the apples not above it.</p>",
