   "slug": "count-in-range",
   "title": "How Many in the Range?",
   "level": 1,
   "statement": "<p>Read a list of numbers, then answer some questions. Each question gives two numbers <code>l</code> and <code>r</code>: how many numbers of the list are between <code>l</code> and <code>r</code>, both included?</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code>; the second line holds <code>n</code> integers. The third line holds <code>q</code>, and each of the next <code>q</code> lines holds <code>l</code> and <code>r</code>.</p>",
   "output": "<p><code>q</code> lines, one answer per question.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n, q ≤ 1000; all numbers are between −10<sup>6</sup> and 10<sup>6</sup>; l ≤ r.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "6\n5 1 9 3 7 3\n3\n3 7\n10 20\n1 1\n",
     "out": "4\n0\n1\n"
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Sort the list once. In a sorted list the numbers inside a range sit next to each other, and <code>bisect</code> can find both edges of that block.</p>",
   "solution": "from bisect import bisect_left, bisect_right\nn = int(input())\na = sorted(map(int, input().split()))\nq = int(input())\nfor _ in range(q):\n    l, r = map(int, input().split())\n    print(bisect_right(a, r) - bisect_left(a, l))",
   "explanation": "",
