   "statement": "<p>Rearrange the letters of a word into alphabetical order, treating capital and small letters as the same letter. When the same letter appears in both forms, the capital ones come before the small ones.</p>",
   "input": "<p>One line with a word made of English letters.</p>",
   "output": "<p>The rearranged word.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>The word has 1 to 1000 letters.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "bAnaNa\n",
     "out": "AaabNn\n"
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Sort with a key that is a pair: the lowercase version of the letter first, and the letter itself second. Why does the second part put <code>A</code> before <code>a</code>?</p>",
   "solution": "s = input().strip()\nprint(''.join(sorted(s, key=lambda c: (c.lower(), c))))",
   "explanation": "",
