   "statement": "<p>Run insertion sort on a list (smallest to largest) and show the list after each insertion step. Step <code>i</code> (for <code>i = 2, 3, …, n</code>) inserts the <code>i</code>-th number into the sorted part made of the first <code>i − 1</code> numbers.</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code>. The second line holds <code>n</code> integers.</p>",
   "output": "<p><code>n − 1</code> lines: the whole list after steps 2, 3, …, <code>n</code>, numbers separated by single spaces. Print a line even when a step moves nothing.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>2 ≤ n ≤ 50; every number is between −100 and 100.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "5\n5 2 4 6 1\n",
     "out": "2 5 4 6 1\n2 4 5 6 1\n2 4 5 6 1\n1 2 4 5 6\n"
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Write ordinary insertion sort and add one <code>print(*a)</code> at the end of each pass of the outer loop.</p>",
   "solution": "n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\nfor i in range(1, n):\n    key = a[i]\n    j = i - 1\n    while j >= 0 and a[j] > key:\n        a[j + 1] = a[j]\n        j -= 1\n    a[j + 1] = key\n    print(*a)",
   "explanation": "",
