   "level": 2,
   "statement": "<p>Players finish a game one after another, and each gets a score. As soon as a player finishes, the screen shows their rank among everyone who has finished so far: 1 plus the number of earlier players with a strictly higher score. Print the rank shown for each player.</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code>. The second line holds the <code>n</code> scores in finishing order.</p>",
   "output": "<p>One line with <code>n</code> ranks separated by single spaces.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n ≤ 500; 0 ≤ score ≤ 10000.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "5\n50 80 80 30 90\n",
     "out": "1 1 1 4 1\n"
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Keep the scores seen so far in a sorted list, inserting each new score the insertion-sort way. The rank comes from how many are bigger.</p>",
   "solution": "n = int(input())\nscores = list(map(int, input().split()))\nboard = []          # sorted from high to low\nout = []\nfor s in scores:\n    board.append(s)\n    j = len(board) - 2\n    while j >= 0 and board[j] < s:\n        board[j + 1] = board[j]\n        j -= 1\n    board[j + 1] = s\n    rank = 1\n    while board[rank - 1] > s:\n        rank += 1\n    out.append(rank)\nprint(*out)",
