   "hint": "<p>Start one pointer at the smallest number and one at the largest. If their sum is too small, which pointer should move? If it is too big?</p>",
   "solution": "n, t = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\ni, j = 0, n - 1\ncount = 0\nwhile i < j:\n    s = a[i] + a[j]\n    if s == t:\n        count += 1\n        i += 1\n        j -= 1\n    elif s < t:\n        i += 1\n    else:\n        j -= 1\nprint(count)",
