   "slug": "pairs-with-difference",
   "title": "Pairs With a Given Gap",
   "level": 3,
   "statement": "<p>A list of <strong>different</strong> integers (in any order) and a number <code>k</code> are given. Count the pairs of numbers from the list whose difference is exactly <code>k</code>. Each pair is counted once.</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code> and <code>k</code>. The second line holds <code>n</code> distinct integers.</p>",
   "output": "<p>One integer: the number of pairs.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n ≤ 1000; 1 ≤ k ≤ 10<sup>6</sup>; all numbers are between −10<sup>6</sup> and 10<sup>6</sup>.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "6 2\n1 5 3 4 2 8\n",
     "out": "3\n",
     "why": "<p>(1, 3), (3, 5) and (2, 4).</p>"
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Sort first. Then keep two pointers <code>i &lt; j</code> that both only move forward: if <code>a[j] − a[i]</code> is too small move <code>j</code>, if it is too big move <code>i</code>.</p>",
   "solution": "n, k = map(int, input().split())\na = sorted(map(int, input().split()))\ni, j = 0, 1\ncount = 0\nwhile j < n:\n    d = a[j] - a[i]\n    if d == k:\n        count += 1\n        i += 1\n        j += 1\n    elif d < k:\n        j += 1\n    else:\n        i += 1\n        if i == j:\n            j += 1\nprint(count)",
