   "slug": "busiest-moment",
   "title": "The Busiest Moment",
   "level": 3,
   "statement": "<p>A museum records when each visitor came in and went out. Visitor <code>i</code> is inside from time <code>a<sub>i</sub></code> up to, but not including, time <code>b<sub>i</sub></code>: someone who leaves at time 5 and someone who arrives at time 5 are never inside together. What is the largest number of visitors inside at the same moment?</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code>. Each of the next <code>n</code> lines holds <code>a<sub>i</sub></code> and <code>b<sub>i</sub></code>.</p>",
   "output": "<p>One integer: the largest number of visitors inside at once.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n ≤ 1000; 0 ≤ a<sub>i</sub> &lt; b<sub>i</sub> ≤ 10<sup>4</sup>.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "4\n1 5\n2 3\n3 7\n5 6\n",
     "out": "2\n"
    },
    {
     "in": "3\n1 10\n2 9\n3 8\n",
     "out": "3\n"
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Make one sorted list of arrival times and one sorted list of leaving times, and merge them with two pointers like a timeline. When an arrival and a departure happen at the same time, handle the departure first.</p>",
   "solution": "n = int(input())\narr, dep = [], []\nfor _ in range(n):\n    a, b = map(int, input().split())\n    arr.append(a)\n    dep.append(b)\narr.sort()\ndep.sort()\ni = j = 0\ninside = best = 0\nwhile i < n:\n    if arr[i] < dep[j]:\n        inside += 1\n        best = max(best, inside)\n        i += 1\n    else:\n        inside -= 1\n        j += 1\nprint(best)",
